1 Overview
**********

Basalt Deep Learning is a portable C++20 deep-learning framework
licensed under the GNU General Public License version 3 or later
(GPLv3+).  It is built on top of the _Bellows_ C++ machine-learning
library and its transitive _Hyper Math_ scientific computing engine.

   Basalt Deep Learning adheres strictly to the GNU Coding Standards as
an engineering, formatting, build-system, and documentation discipline.
It is an independent project and is *not* part of, endorsed by, or
affiliated with the GNU Project.

1.1 Key Capabilities
====================

   • Multi-dtype N-dimensional strided ‘basalt::Tensor’ with zero-copy
     views and NumPy/PyTorch-compatible broadcasting over Bellows
     ‘slab_buffer’ arenas.
   • Dynamic reverse-mode automatic differentiation with higher-order
     derivatives (‘create_graph = true’), ‘No_Grad_Guard’,
     ‘Enable_Grad_Guard’, activation ‘checkpoint’, and finite-difference
     ‘gradcheck’.
   • Comprehensive ‘basalt::nn’ module library including ‘Linear’,
     ‘Conv1d’/‘2d’/‘3d’, pooling, ‘Batch_Norm’, ‘Layer_Norm’,
     ‘Group_Norm’, ‘RMS_Norm’, ‘Multihead_Attention’,
     ‘Transformer_Encoder’, and ‘Transformer_Decoder’.
   • First-order and adaptive optimizers (‘SGD’, ‘Adam’, ‘AdamW’,
     ‘RMSprop’, ‘Adagrad’, ‘LAMB’) and learning-rate schedulers
     (‘Step_LR’, ‘Cosine_Annealing_LR’, ‘One_Cycle_LR’,
     ‘Linear_Warmup_LR’, ‘Reduce_LR_On_Plateau’).
   • Versioned FNV-1a checksummed checkpoints (‘.bckpt’), Hugging Face
     Safetensors (‘.safetensors’), and ONNX (‘.onnx’) import/export.
   • Lightning-style ‘basalt::Trainer’, mixed precision (‘Float16’ and
     ‘BFloat16’), multi-device ‘Data_Parallel’, a stable C ABI
     (‘libbasalt-c’), CLI utilities (‘basalt-train’, ‘basalt-inspect’,
     ‘basalt-convert’), and optional ‘pybind11’ Python bindings (‘import
     basalt’).


