5 Tensors and Operations
************************

 -- Struct: basalt::Tensor_Options
     Configuration struct holding ‘dtype’, ‘device’, and ‘requires_grad’
     for tensor creation.

 -- Class: basalt::Tensor
     Multi-dtype N-dimensional strided tensor handle backed by
     ‘Bellows_Storage’.  Provides zero-copy view methods (‘view’,
     ‘reshape’, ‘transpose’, ‘t’, ‘permute’, ‘slice’, ‘narrow’,
     ‘select’, ‘squeeze’, ‘unsqueeze’, ‘expand’, ‘broadcast_to’,
     ‘flatten’), device/dtype transfer (‘to’, ‘cpu’, ‘cuda’,
     ‘contiguous’, ‘clone’, ‘detach’), in-place mutations (‘fill_’,
     ‘zero_’, ‘copy_’, ‘add_’, ‘mul_’), and autograd methods
     (‘backward’, ‘grad’, ‘set_requires_grad’, ‘retain_grad’,
     ‘zero_grad’).

 -- Function: basalt::Tensor basalt::zeros (const Shape_Vector &SHAPE,
          Tensor_Options OPTIONS)
     Factory functions constructing tensors on CPU or CUDA and bridging
     to and from ‘bellows::data_table’.

 -- Function: basalt::Tensor basalt::ops::matmul (const Tensor &A, const
          Tensor &B)
     Differentiable mathematical, reduction, linear-algebra, and
     indexing operations in ‘basalt::ops’.


